    "description": "I have held a number of roles in my career at Microsoft. I am currently a developer in the CoreAI org delivering the Github Copilot CLI, the Github Copilot Coding Agent as well as other agentic development scenarios. Previously, I was the architect for Github Copilot for Azure which provided the AI access to Azure resources for management and code generation. This has now evolved in the Azure MCP. I was an architect in the .Net Developer Tools org and I spent a few years as an architect and manager in Azure working on Core Azure Networking and the hosted Redis product. Before that, I was Architect and Developer on the Visual Studio Diagnostics team for 20 years. My responsibilities in that role included designing and implementing critical components of Microsoft's Diagnostics stack including the debugger, historical debugger, Azure cloud debugger, Android Emulator, and performance tools. In this role I had the opportunity to work at all layers of the stack including consuming raw compiler outputs, assisting hardware vendors creating diagnostic support in their hardware, and changes in the OS kernels, I have nearly 40 patents.",
